eplace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Weigh the observed-read-set-as-dependency-set mechanism against the established auto-dependency-discovery prior art (gcc -MD/automake, redo, read-tracing memoizers) and state how the design bounds its characteristic under-approximation / fail-open hazard (a depended-on file read via an untraced path being dropped from the set).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The plan grounds the CONTENT-HASH core in ADR-0002 (which itself cites Bazel/Nix/git/Gerrit/proof-caching), but the read-set-from-telemetry mechanism is a distinct architectural choice presented with only first-principles reasoning ('read_set_recorded is set ONLY when a fetch was OBSERVED ... the stronger reading would scope fail-OPEN').","Retrieved prior art: automake/gcc -MD compute a dependency list from the headers a compile actually read; redo and fabricate/memoize track observed file accesses to decide rebuilds — an established class the plan reinvents in miniature.","The class's known pitfall — a real dependency the tooling did not observe is silently dropped, yielding a stale-but-current result — is precisely the fail-open direction the plan's own existence-filter and empty-observation reasoning circle without naming as prior art.","Confirmed the read-set filter keeps only read_file targets and drops search_files/list_directory (read_set.py:120-158): files a review grounded on via those tools, or via any untraced access, never enter the dependency set."],"finding":"The novel axis of this design — deriving the attestation-currency dependency set from OBSERVED fetch telemetry (distinct_fetches / the read-set) rather than declared or cited inputs — is not weighed against the established prior-art class for exactly this pattern (auto-dependency discovery from observed file reads: gcc -MD/automake, redo, and read-tracing memoizers like fabricate/memoize), and so does not confront that class's defining hazard: under-approximation / fail-open when a genuinely-depended-on file was read via a path the telemetry did not capture, leaving the attestation falsely current.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9697acd4a6bac25f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section (a) 'Record the read-set inside the signed material' and (b) composition rule; read_set.normalize_read_set","norm_id":"n251db825ad8a066b","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A review substantively depends on a file it surfaced via search_files or a tool whose target is not a read_file path; that file is excluded from the read-set, so a later content change to it does not invalidate the attestation.","Telemetry misses or coalesces a read the review relied on; the omitted file's drift goes undetected under read-set scoping."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a short prior-art paragraph to plan section (a) or the ADR addendum: name the observed-read tracking class, note that read-set scoping shares its under-approximation hazard, and argue the containment — e.g. the blast-radius entries (criteria/routing/rubrics/gates/rebar.toml) plus the ADR-0002 material-fingerprint binding cover the config-level drift that read_file telemetry cannot, and that residual per-file under-approximation degrades toward the same whole-HEAD fail-safe rather than silently exempting drift.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes",